# RFC-TM-6 §4 (rfc-tm-6-diamond.md): goldens/live/ is regenerated by every
# `pnpm run test` from the flipped renderer — build output the classifier
# (check-golden-deltas.mjs) reads, not committed source. goldens/legacy-baseline/
# is the pinned, committed artifact; goldens/live/ never is.
lib/typed-mind-renderer/goldens/live/

# PR #156 — ladder fixture 81 is a two-package mini-workspace that reproduces a
# pnpm `workspace:*` resolution gap. Its sibling's `dist/index.d.ts` is FIXTURE
# INPUT, not build output: `ts.resolveModuleName` only reports
# `isExternalLibraryImport: true` (the misclassification the fixture pins) when
# the specifier resolves through a node_modules link to the package's declared
# `types` entry. Nothing in this repo builds that file, so the blanket `dist/`
# rule above would leave the fixture non-hermetic and the test would pass
# locally while failing on a clean runner. The negation re-includes exactly
# that one path. The matching node_modules link is created by the test's own
# setup step (fixtures cannot rely on a committed symlink working on every
# platform), so no `node_modules/` negation is needed.
!lib/typed-mind-typescript/tests/ladder/repros-analyzer/81-crosspkg-type-only-dto-field/packages/core/dist/
!lib/typed-mind-typescript/tests/ladder/repros-analyzer/81-crosspkg-type-only-dto-field/packages/core/dist/**
